{"answer":"A review of the raw data established that the published delta efficiency (DE) values in the Armstrong paper were calculated using the wrong equation.

Using the correct equation, we recalculated Armstrong's DE as 23.55% in January 1993 (23.02% if the 2-min stage is included), which exceeds the 23.12% value for the final test in November 1999. This is 8% higher than the reported value of 21.75%.

